Setting default timeout values for all resources in a Terraform module can help ensure consistent behavior across different environments. You can achieve this by defining a default timeout variable in your module and then applying it to each resource within the module.

### Step-by-Step Guide to Set Default Timeout Values

1. **Define Default Timeout Variable**:
   Define a default timeout variable in your module's `variables.tf` file.

2. **Apply Default Timeout to Resources**:
   Use the default timeout variable in the `timeouts` block for each resource in your module.

3. **Override Default Timeout if Needed**:
   Allow for overriding the default timeout value when the module is called, if necessary.

### Example Terraform Module with Default Timeouts

#### Directory Structure

```
terraform/
|-- modules/
|   |-- ingestion/
|   |   |-- main.tf
|   |   |-- variables.tf
|   |   |-- outputs.tf
|-- main.tf
|-- variables.tf
|-- outputs.tf
```

#### Define Default Timeout Variable

In the `variables.tf` file of your module, define a default timeout variable.

##### `modules/ingestion/variables.tf`

```hcl
variable "default_timeout" {
  description = "Default timeout value for all resources in the module."
  type        = string
  default     = "10m"
}
```

#### Apply Default Timeout to Resources

In the `main.tf` file of your module, apply the default timeout to each resource.

##### `modules/ingestion/main.tf`

```hcl
resource "aws_s3_bucket" "ingestion_bucket" {
  bucket = var.bucket_name
  acl    = "private"
  timeouts {
    create = var.default_timeout
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "ingestion_role" {
  name = var.role_name

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "lambda.amazonaws.com"
        }
      },
    ]
  })
  timeouts {
    create = var.default_timeout
  }
}
```

#### Override Default Timeout if Needed

When calling the module, you can override the default timeout value if necessary.

##### `main.tf`

```hcl
module "ingestion" {
  source = "./modules/ingestion"

  bucket_name = "my-ingestion-bucket"
  role_name   = "my-ingestion-role"
  default_timeout = "15m"  # Override the default timeout if needed
}
```

### Full Example

Here is the full example with all the pieces together:

#### `modules/ingestion/variables.tf`

```hcl
variable "bucket_name" {
  description = "Name of the S3 bucket."
  type        = string
}

variable "role_name" {
  description = "Name of the IAM role."
  type        = string
}

variable "default_timeout" {
  description = "Default timeout value for all resources in the module."
  type        = string
  default     = "10m"
}
```

